{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The HDMI cable was a partial match because my DVI cable purchase suggests that connecting displays can be relevant to me, although I would need a specific HDMI connection to make before choosing it."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Fire TV devices and Echo products introduce entertainment or voice-assistant uses that my purchases do not show me seeking.",
    "My small-tablet mount served a specific mounting purpose; it does not mean I need a GoPro chest mount or another tablet.",
    "The memory card would only be useful if I had a compatible device needing more storage, and I have no current need for that."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying electronics seems to have been treated as interest in many kinds of electronic devices, even though my purchases mostly solve particular connection or accessory needs.",
    "Several streaming devices repeat the same assumption that I want TV entertainment equipment, without a clear connection to my history."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest purchase was a USB-to-Ethernet adapter, which points more directly toward practical computer connectivity than toward streaming or smart-home devices.",
    "The connector, device compatibility, and exact task matter to me more than whether an item is broadly related to electronics.",
    "My purchases are spread far apart, and I rarely interact unless something addresses a concrete need; an accessory purchase does not imply an ongoing desire for related equipment."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized a broad interest in electronics but missed my more specific pattern of occasional purchases for practical connectivity needs."
}"}
